1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,540
Bye, thanks for being my models for a little while.

2
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:18,520
What do you mean I can't go on this one?

3
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:19,860
Yuko, calm down.

4
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,080
I want to perform in more guerrilla concerts.

5
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:25,880
Sorry, but the concert on Akibastar overlaps with it.

6
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:29,120
Yuko, you'll be taking over Achan's position.

7
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:31,920
Akibastar's just some boring planet.

8
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:34,140
But I want to get out of here.

9
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:37,280
I want to sing on a bigger stage for even more people.

10
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:38,560
Take that back.

11
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:42,000
Akibastar is special.

12
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:47,700
A long time ago, it was ravaged by terrible wars that plunged it into poverty and ruin.

13
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:52,020
But the people still love their planet dearly.

14
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:55,680
They spent generations creating the subterranean city.

15
00:00:55,680 --> 00:01:02,120
This place embraces painful situations and sad memories and gives birth to new hope.

16
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:06,900
That's why people who come to Akibastar love entertainment.

17
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:10,360
It's not some boring planet.

18
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:16,840
Akibastar and the 0048 stage, they are our most important and sacred space.

19
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:19,280
I'm sorry.

20
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:23,880
Yuko, protect the glow of Akibastar for me.

21
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:25,760
The glow of Akibastar?

22
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:26,880
Yes.

23
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:30,260
In order to do that, you yourself must shine.

24
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:36,320
If you let it, Akibastar will shine down on you and make you glow even brighter.

25
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:38,220
I can't wait to see it.

26
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:43,320
It's not fair, Akibastar.

27
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:50,500
You told me to protect Akibastar and then ran off somewhere that I couldn't follow.

28
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:57,760
But there is something I can do now.

29
00:01:57,760 --> 00:02:27,740
It's not fair, Akibastar.

30
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:30,740
In here, I wonder why she inherited Mariko in the first place.

31
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:35,220
The other successors seem inspired to dance better.

32
00:02:35,540 --> 00:02:36,920
Especially Chan-Yu.

33
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:38,800
She's really getting into it.

34
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,460
Yeah, that's my girl.

35
00:02:45,060 --> 00:02:47,280
The trainees seem excited, too.

36
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:50,420
Lately, Nagichie has been showing progress.

37
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:51,360
Great progress.

38
00:02:51,360 --> 00:03:01,140
All the other members sparkle when a center nova is about to be born.

39
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:04,820
That excites you?

40
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:05,200
Huh?

41
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:07,540
Don't you remember what you said?

42
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:14,100
If it's truly your intention to bring back the center nova position, I'll do everything I can to stop you.

43
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:17,000
Don't tell me you're going back on your work.

44
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:18,360
Oh, come on, Tsubasa.

45
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:21,380
Did you forget I used to be a member of Zero Zero?

46
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:24,360
The members' hearts are always one, remember?

47
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:27,540
There's no need to be distant.

48
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:29,760
I still feel the same way as you.

49
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:30,720
Probably.

50
00:03:30,720 --> 00:03:38,700
Great progress, what a good job!

51
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:40,760
Come on, we gotta hustle!

52
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:42,060
Okay.

53
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:43,960
Don't leave without me!

54
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:46,080
Wait up!

55
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:48,180
Mariko, you're a successor now.

56
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:50,200
Shouldn't you be going home on the bus with the others?

57
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:52,380
I wanted to take the train home.

58
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:56,140
Mariko, you shouldn't do something like this.

59
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:58,940
Successors shouldn't spend so much time with trainees.

60
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:05,380
Whether someone is a successor or trainee doesn't matter to me.

61
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:08,600
If I want to ride the train with you guys, I'm going to do it!

62
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:10,120
Wow!

63
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:13,020
Mariko-sama, you sounded like a sadist just then!

64
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:14,860
That gave me chills.

65
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,400
No fair!

66
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:18,860
Mima, Mari, tease me too!

67
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:20,080
Tease me, tease me!

68
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:22,740
Um, that sounds really weird!

69
00:04:24,740 --> 00:04:27,280
This isn't that how you try this train is for us.

70
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:27,620
Ready up.

71
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:28,080
Huh?

72
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:28,800
Huh?

73
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:30,120
It's Yuko!

74
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:31,580
Uh, Yuko-san?

75
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:31,980
Where?

76
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:32,400
Where?

77
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:33,400
Over there!

78
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:34,220
By the turbine!

79
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:37,540
I-I see someone, but I can't tell if it's Yuko.

80
00:04:37,660 --> 00:04:39,480
Sona does got Hawkeyes on her.

81
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:42,260
Well, if it is her, what is she doing over there?

82
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:55,440
Yuko-san.

83
00:04:55,440 --> 00:04:58,160
She really has an amazing voice, doesn't she?

84
00:04:58,160 --> 00:04:58,800
Hold up.

85
00:04:58,800 --> 00:04:58,820
Hold up.

86
00:04:58,820 --> 00:04:59,760
You can hear her?

87
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:00,620
Mm-hmm.

88
00:05:00,620 --> 00:05:03,800
Now that you mention it, so can I.

89
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:07,960
Even now I can hear the wind sink, the ground in life's new beginning.

90
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,860
She must really be belting it.

91
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:12,840
I can't believe we can hear her over the sound of the turbine.

92
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:16,300
And she's hitting the notes perfectly despite all of the rumbling.

93
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:19,220
I can feel all of Yuko-san's emotion.

94
00:05:19,220 --> 00:05:19,640
What?

95
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:20,880
What do you mean?

96
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:25,160
Even though she took first place at the general elections, she's not satisfied.

97
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:28,460
It's as though she's shouting that she wants to reach even higher.

98
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:29,460
But...

99
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:34,300
What's wrong, Nagisa?

100
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:37,800
She's too cool.

101
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:37,960
Huh?

102
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:39,600
Darn it!

103
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:43,840
Maybe it was a bad idea to take down the pictures of her I had in my room!

104
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:47,840
I need to find new ones to hang up in front of!

105
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:50,840
I have a new holo of Yuko-san if you'd like to have it.

106
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:51,840
Huh?

107
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:55,840
As long as you don't mind a holo card with Makoto-san on the back, you're welcome to it.

108
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:56,840
Oh!

109
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:58,840
Suzuko!

110
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:03,840
Even now I can hear the world sing, calling for a new beginning.

111
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:08,840
And in the sea of despair, we will not drown.

112
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:09,840
Stop!

113
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:10,840
Kojuharu, you're behind!

114
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:11,840
Sorry!

115
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:12,840
Mariko, look around yourself.

116
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:13,840
