Oh!

141
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:38,840
Oh!

142
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:41,840
The ace suddenly left practice.

143
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:44,840
You never know when you'll have the opportunity for a good photo.

144
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:47,840
She's unbelievable.

145
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:49,840
But she's certainly got the energy.

146
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:50,840
Guess I'll let it slide.

147
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:52,840
Yuko-san!

148
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:53,840
Huh?

149
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:04,840
Yuko-san!

150
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:05,840
Huh?

151
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:10,840
Huh?

152
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:24,840
Uh-huh!

153
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:25,840
Uh-huh!

154
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:26,840
Uh-huh!

155
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:27,840
Uh-huh.

156
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:32,840
These days she usually acts like her normal self, but sometimes she's difficult to approach.

157
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:35,840
Just like she was tonight.

158
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:37,840
It's like she's become a...

159
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:39,840
She's become a what?

160
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:41,840
A warrior.

161
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:44,840
If that makes sense.

162
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:47,840
I've seen this behavior before.

163
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:48,840
Huh?

164
00:07:48,840 --> 00:07:50,840
Someone like her.

165
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:53,840
She laughs with everyone, and is loved by all.

166
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:57,840
But she… she's not that easy to approach most of the time.

167
00:07:57,840 --> 00:08:02,840
Even when she's with everyone else, somehow she seems alone.

168
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:04,840
You must be talking about Achan.

169
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,840
Huh? Tsubasa-san?

170
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:12,840
The 13th generation Achan was like that for a while after she became the Center Nova.

171
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:21,840
She had an aura that kept people away, and prevented them from speaking to her freely.

172
00:08:23,840 --> 00:08:29,840
Achan, I… I feel like you're becoming increasingly alone.

173
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:31,840
Alone? Why's that?

174
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:33,840
I don't know.

175
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,840
I don't even know why I feel that way.

176
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:40,840
But… everyone here really likes you.

177
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:43,840
If there's something we can help with, just ask.

178
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:47,840
I feel like you're fighting on your own. You can rely on us.

179
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:53,840
Thanks. That means a lot.

180
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:58,840
I like everyone else as well. I love them.

181
00:08:58,840 --> 00:09:02,840
Thank you for worrying about me, Mariko. I'll work on it.

182
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:03,840
Achan…

183
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:08,840
Don't worry. I know that I'm not alone here. So smile for me.

184
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:10,840
But…

185
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:14,840
But…

186
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:20,840
Achan disappeared immediately after that conversation.

187
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:27,840
Where did the Center Novus disappear to?

188
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:30,840
That's the question on everyone's mind.

189
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:36,840
If you could see them again, it would be…

190
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:47,840
And make this broken world of space before…

191
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:49,840
You scared me half to death!

192
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:53,840
And my evil plan to feel your youthful skin is working out nicely!

193
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:54,840
Holy crap, it's tight!

194
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:58,840
If you're gonna fondle, at least put on a towel or something first!

195
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:03,840
Loneliness for us is the price that we all must pay for freedom!

196
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:04,840
Huh?

197
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:05,840
Hey, Yuko.

198
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:08,840
Do you still want to go there, even if the cost is great?

199
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:10,840
It's closer than you realize.

200
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:11,840
Huh?

201
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:13,840
Somewhere no one will bother you.

202
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:16,840
The sacred position zero.

203
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:20,840
Position zero?

204
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:28,840
Buried deep within Archibastar is a massive duolinium deposit.

205
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:33,840
But greater than that is the Center Nova, the goddess of the sun,

206
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:37,840
who activates the duolinium and makes the Kuraras shine intensely bright.

207
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:42,840
I'm so grateful for the miracle that's about to occur.

208
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:44,840
I may just sing myself.

209
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:49,840
One, two, three, four!

210
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:56,840
I want you!

211
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:58,840
I need you!

212
00:10:58,840 --> 00:10:59,840
I want you!

213
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:00,840
I need you!

214
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:01,840
I need you!

215
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:02,840
I love you!

216
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:03,840
I love you!

217
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:04,840
I love you!

218
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:07,800
Atama no nagante lur crafts

219
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:18,840
Music heavy in off the screen!

220
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:21,840
Ryuko-san shining out there!

221
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:23,840
Oh, her stage presence is overwhelming!

222
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:26,340
She might really be able to become the Center Nova.

223
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:30,640
But if she becomes the Center Nova...

224
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:33,840
At the general elections, she said she wouldn't disappear on us.

225
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:36,040
She'll be fine. I know she will.

226
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:44,540
The first condition for triggering the Center Nova phenomenon...

227
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:46,340
A concert on Akibastar.

228
00:11:53,840 --> 00:12:03,840
To be continued...

229
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:20,840
If you want to become the Center Nova, you have to accept the burden of solitude.

230
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:21,840
Solitude?

231
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:25,840
Those who shine bright are always followed by dark shadows.

232
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:30,220
Fued with jealousy, targeted and constantly used.

233
00:12:33,900 --> 00:12:38,220
Position Zero wholeheartedly takes on all of these headwinds.

234
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:43,260
But if you're courageous enough to seize that darkness and make it your own,

235
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:45,780
the position you want to be will also be yours.

236
00:12:45,780 --> 00:12:51,340
I want you, I want you, I need you, I need you.

237
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:52,600
There's no one there.

238
00:12:54,740 --> 00:12:57,680
Back then, Ah-chan was always right before me.

239
00:12:58,380 --> 00:13:01,080
She may have been protecting me from those strong winds.

240
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:03,940
I didn't even know they were there to begin with.

241
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:07,020
But now, she's not there anymore.

242
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:09,660
And it's my turn to step into the wind.

243
00:13:09,660 --> 00:13:22,220
This is an emergency.

244
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:26,120
Presidents of Akibastar should evacuate to shelters immediately.

245
00:13:26,520 --> 00:13:27,060
Evaculate?

246
00:13:27,060 --> 00:13:28,280
What's going on up there?

247
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:29,200
Listen up, everyone.

248
00:13:29,740 --> 00:13:33,260
A massive DES force has crossed our defensive line and is invading.

249
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:35,680
The trainees have already moved out.

250
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:36,860
Follow them.

251
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:38,340
Right.

252
00:13:39,660 --> 00:13:48,560
The second condition for triggering the Sintanova phenomenon.

253
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:50,920
A concert with some bad weather.

254
00:13:58,060 --> 00:14:00,620
Hey, where is all this lightning coming from?

255
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:03,700
It's possible that the weather control system was hacked by enemy forces.

256
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:04,560
For real?

257
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:06,280
Something's very wrong.

258
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:08,960
This is definitely not the Akibastar, I know.

259
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:09,460
Oh!

260
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:14,300
They're here.

261
00:14:14,780 --> 00:14:15,160
Oh!

262
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:16,280
Let's go, everyone!

263
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:18,940
Protect the planet and the fan!

264
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:20,960
Oh, no!

265
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:29,960
No!

266
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:30,460
No!

267
00:14:30,460 --> 00:14:30,960
No!

268
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:31,460
No!

269
00:14:31,460 --> 00:14:32,460
This is wrong!

270
00:14:32,460 --> 00:14:32,960
This isn't what they promised!

271
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:33,460
